      "word_count": 6971,
      "summary": "Experimental study (Hospital del Mar Barcelona; 70 Balb/c mice, 7 groups, Vaccines 10(4):594) testing whether re-frozen leftover COVID-19 mRNA vaccine retains integrity and immunogenicity. Reconstituted (diluted) Comirnaty and Spikevax drawn into syringes were stored 1 month at -20 C or -80 C, thawed refrigerated, then injected IM: mRNA integrity was unaffected by either condition, murine immune responses matched freshly prepared controls, and no adverse signs appeared (body weight, Irwin observational test, locomotor activity). This is the closest controlled empirical head-to-head of -20 C versus -80 C storage for commercial COVID-19 mRNA vaccines in indexed literature. Caveat: it tested diluted vaccine in syringes over 1 month, not multi-month undiluted-depot storage, so it complements rather than replaces regulatory dossier stability tables.",
      "created": "2026-08-23T12:35:53.202145+00:00",
      "updated": "2026-08-23T12:40:09.026009+00:00"
