      "word_count": 9002,
      "summary": "Perspective study (Zoltan Kis, Univ. Sheffield, Pharmaceutics 14(2):430) proposing an Arrhenius first-order kinetic framework to quantify mRNA-vaccine stability-related CQAs and remaining shelf life from distribution temperature logs. Tabulates approved depot and handling conditions: BNT162b2 original PBS formulation -90 to -60 C up to 6 months, transport/storage -25 to -15 C (commonly -20 C) up to 2 weeks, 2-8 C up to 1 month, 6 h post-dilution at 8-25 C; BNT162b2 Tris reformulation 10 weeks at 2-8 C and 12 h at 2-30 C post-puncture; mRNA-1273 6 months at -50 to -15 C (commonly -20 C), 30 days at 2-8 C, 24 h total at 8-25 C. Cites Pfizer-derived models and Moderna statements that mRNA degradation follows Arrhenius behavior with first-order kinetics, enabling extrapolation from accelerated high-temperature data to subzero depots. No new empirical potency data.",
