      "summary": "EMA CHMP initial-MA assessment report for Comirnaty: finished-product 6-month shelf life at -90/-60°C rested on 'limited stability data' (one clinical batch + one non-clinical batch); drug substance approved at -20±5°C; accelerated (-40 to +5°C) and stressed (+25/+30°C) data existed; REC22 directed investigation toward -20°C long-term storage and longer 2-8°C in-use windows; one thaw-refreeze cycle allowed in transport; dry-ice shipper defined the temperature envelope.",
