      "summary": "Oude Blenke, Örnskov, Schöneich, Nilsson, Volkin, Mastrobattista, Almarsson & Crommelin (J Pharm Sci 2023), 'The Storage and In-Use Stability of mRNA Vaccines and Therapeutics: Not A Cold Case' — the authoritative pharma-science review of why mRNA-LNP drug products need frozen storage and what could end it. Key findings: (1) degradation chemistry — 2'-OH transesterification strand scission accelerates with alkaline pH and heat (>100-fold rate variation by sequence/site), minimized around pH 7 and at −20/−70°C; depurination/deamination negligible when stored frozen at neutral pH; (2) LNPs are a double-edged sword — they shield mRNA from RNases but PEG-lipid hydroperoxides and ionizable-lipid N-oxide→aldehyde pathways form covalent mRNA-lipid adducts that correlate negatively with protein expression (Packer et al.), so adduct testing is now expected in every stability protocol; (3) deployment-era breakthroughs — Comirnaty's phosphate 'purple cap' buffer was replaced with Tris ('gray cap'), which doubles as an aldehyde sink, extending 2–8°C shelf life from 1 month to 10 weeks while retaining −80°C depot storage; Spikevax (Tris from the start, but −20°C long-term) still gets only 30 days refrigerated; EMA noted Moderna's degradataion follows Arrhenius first-order kinetics enabling excursion modelling; (4) routes off the deep-freeze chain — secondary-structure design (AUP minimization gave 2-fold spike-RNA stabilization), shortened 1100-nt mRNA keeping 76% intact after 6 months at 2–8°C (Zhao et al.), oxidation-resistant branched saturated ionizable-lipid tails, lyophilization (GEMCOVAC-19 authorized in India; DOTAP-NLC lyophile active after 21 months at 4°C; Moderna CMV vaccine in Phase 3 lyophilized), spray drying, and point-of-use kit assembly (BioNTainer, Lipo-MERIT). (5) in-use reality: mechanical shear (shaking/dropping), not thermal excursions within tested ranges, is the acute killer; punctured vials' 12-hour limit is sterility-driven. NOTE id/title 'acknowledgement' came from JATS XML auto-parse.",
