      "summary": "FDA press announcement, February 25, 2021 — primary regulatory document updating the Pfizer-BioNTech COVID-19 Vaccine Fact Sheet for Healthcare Providers. Permits undiluted frozen vials to be transported and stored at conventional pharmaceutical-freezer temperatures for up to two weeks as an alternative to the preferred -80°C to -60°C ultra-low freezer storage, based on stability data submitted by Pfizer. Preserves prior handling rules: thawed undiluted vials keep up to 5 days refrigerated; after dilution, vials keep 6 hours at refrigerator or room temperature. CBER director Peter Marks frames the change as easing the burden of procuring ultra-low cold-storage equipment and extending reach to more vaccination sites — the first major US regulatory relaxation of the mRNA vaccine cold chain.",
