      "summary": "Khan, Islam, Mishra & Kamen 2026 comprehensive review of mRNA-LNP degradation mechanisms (Vaccines 14(7):620, doi:10.3390/vaccines14070620; PMC mirror fetched after MDPI bot wall). Post-pandemic thermostability synthesis: instability factors are temperature (Arrhenius-accelerated backbone hydrolysis), pH, light, oxidation, aggregation, shear stress, humidity, and freeze-thaw cycles; degradation pathways include phosphodiester hydrolysis, lipid oxidation/hydrolysis, RNase contamination, poly(A) tail loss, and LNP aggregation/leakage. Documents the regulatory drift from ultra-cold to refrigerated: current labels Comirnaty -90 to -60°C frozen but up to 10 weeks at 2-8°C post-thaw and Spikevax -50 to -15°C with 60 days at 2-8°C, versus original Pfizer-below--70°C/Moderna-below--20°C requirements. Key numbers: without cryoprotectants 2-3 freeze-thaw cycles cut potency >50%; unprotected LNPs in PBS lose near-complete delivery efficacy after two freeze-thaw cycles; lyophilization enables 2-8°C storage for weeks-to-months but no licensed lyophilized mRNA vaccine exists yet; C12-200 LNP formulation held expression 11 weeks even at 25°C while SM-102 failed at 25°C (formulation-dependent thermostability); larger 120-150 nm particles degrade DSPC/cholesterol within 6 months at 4°C.",
