      "summary": "Hou, Zaks, Langer & Dong 2021 Nature Reviews Materials review 'Lipid nanoparticles for mRNA delivery' (doi:10.1038/s41578-021-00358-0; PMC mirror fetched after cookie wall). Authoritative mechanism + clinical-translation review from the Langer/Dong labs covering LNP design (ionizable lipid, cholesterol, helper phospholipid, PEG-lipid), physiological barriers, GMP manufacture, and a dedicated Stability and storage section: both authorized COVID-19 mRNA vaccines are frozen with sucrose cryoprotectant — mRNA-1273 at -15°C to -20°C (inject after thaw) vs BNT162b2 at -60°C to -80°C (thaw plus saline dilution); EMA approved BNT162b2 storage at -15°C to -25°C for 2 weeks on new stability data; 5% sucrose/trehalose in liquid nitrogen preserves delivery efficacy >=3 months in vivo. Mechanism anchors: m1psi nucleoside substitution reduces innate immune sensing; two-proline prefusion-spike stabilization; cholesterol modulates membrane rigidity; PEG-lipids curb aggregation. Argues cold-chain-free LNP formulations would cut production/transport cost and speed vaccination.",
