 ## 2. The Stability Problem: Why RNA Resisted Real-World Deployment
 
-Each ribose carries a 2′-hydroxyl enabling transesterification — the oxygen attacks the adjacent phosphodiester bond, snapping the strand — a reaction accelerated by alkaline pH and heat, Arrhenius-governed (rates rise predictably with temperature), varying over 100-fold site to site, and minimized near pH 7 in an ordinary −20 °C-class freezer rather than anywhere colder [[acknowledgement]]. Potency compounds this: one break anywhere stops that transcript's translation, making integrity all-or-nothing per molecule [[references-2]]. The vehicle helps biology and hurts storage: oxidizing ionizable lipids shed aldehydes forming mRNA-lipid adducts that correlate negatively with expression, while structural modeling puts the particle core near 24 percent water — the hydrolysis substrate ships inside the product [[acknowledgement]] [[data-availability-statement]]. The fragility was real and multi-pathway; nothing in it demanded −80 °C.
+Each ribose carries a 2′-hydroxyl enabling transesterification — the oxygen attacks the adjacent phosphodiester bond, snapping the strand — a reaction accelerated by alkaline pH and heat, Arrhenius-governed, varying over 100-fold site to site, and minimized near pH 7 in an ordinary −20 °C-class freezer rather than anywhere colder [[acknowledgement]]. Potency compounds this: one break anywhere stops that transcript's translation, making integrity all-or-nothing per molecule [[references-2]]. The vehicle helps biology and hurts storage: oxidizing ionizable lipids shed aldehydes forming mRNA-lipid adducts that correlate negatively with expression, while structural modeling puts the particle core near 24 percent water — the hydrolysis substrate ships inside the product [[acknowledgement]] [[data-availability-statement]]. The fragility was real and multi-pathway; nothing in it demanded −80 °C.
 
 ## 3. Sequence-Level Breakthroughs: Nucleoside Modification, Cap Engineering, and Codon Design
 
 Sequence-level engineering edits the transcript's letters — swapped bases, recoded codons, reshaped folds — and earned everything except shelf life. Without m1Ψ no deployable product exists at any temperature: the twentyfold gain above made tolerable doses and fast pivotal trials possible. Storage is another column. The authoritative pharmaceutical-science review declines the tempting equation: modified nucleosides improve translation and immunogenicity profiles "but do not, by themselves, confer chemical stability against hydrolysis" — m1Ψ swaps a base, not the backbone [[lock-2]]. Linkage-level help is sign-unpredictable: probing found uridine-upstream hotspots that Ψ/m1Ψ mitigates, yet mO5U worsened thermal stability versus plain uridine, and no controlled liquid-formulation m1Ψ-versus-unmodified shelf-life trial exists anywhere indexed across 2005–2026 [[acknowledgement]]. The era's natural experiment agrees: CureVac's CVnCoV claimed three months refrigerated on completely unmodified uridines — though its European rolling review (data evaluated as they arrive) was withdrawn unfinished, leaving a manufacturer claim, not endorsed data [[references-2]] [[lock-3]]. Verdict: decisive viability and timing credit; single digits to at most ten percent direct storage credit.

