 ## 4. Formulation-Level Breakthroughs: LNP Encapsulation and Frozen-Stability Engineering
 
 Formulation chemistry changes what the molecule experiences in the vial, and is where margin was physically created. Sucrose was load-bearing: unprotected particles lose over half their potency within two to three freeze–thaw cycles as ice concentrates salts into rupturing pockets, making multi-dose frozen distribution at pandemic scale impossible without cryoprotection — both products shipped frozen in sucrose from day one [[lock-2]]. The Tris swap followed: Comirnaty's phosphate buffer shifts pH catastrophically during freezing, and reformulation into Tris (tromethamine) earned a refrigerated extension "from up to 1 month, to 10 weeks" — roughly 3.3×, the largest chemistry-attributable multiplier, twin-engined by resistance to freeze-induced pH drift and sacrificial scavenging of aldehydes before they adduct the RNA [[acknowledgement]]. The record supplies its control: Spikevax carried Tris from inception yet held thirty refrigerated days because its −20 °C depot left less headroom to spend, while Tris-era products hold the field's best refrigerated allowances through the 2025–26 labels [[acknowledgement]] [[lock-2]]. Then the filings: February 2021 allowed conventional-freezer storage explicitly on data Pfizer submitted, and May 2021 lifted the thawed window five days to one month on reviewed refrigerated results — zero change to the vial either time [[coronavirus-covid-19-update-fda-allows-more-flexible-storage-transportation-cond]] [[fda-extends-pfizer-biontech-vaccine-storage-time-to-30-days]]. Chemistry created margin; dossiers converted it. Booking both as breakthroughs is category error.

