-The strongest counter-frame earns its answer: a dossier cannot alter a rate constant — certification without creation explains nothing about why margin existed, creation without certification explains nothing about when labels moved. Both shares answer different counterfactuals. Motive remains inference — prudence's best leg is neutron-measured crystallization onset at −58 °C in the actual product [[lock-4]], though the same study found mobility rising at least fiftyfold after one melt–refreeze while conceding no quick mRNA degradation followed, and Grau's team re-froze diluted Comirnaty and Spikevax for a month at −20 °C and −80 °C with mRNA integrity and mouse immunogenicity intact against fresh controls [[lock-6]] — a one-month, in-syringe result in unresolved tension with that morphology signal. One ceiling applies, stated once: Pfizer's module 3.2.P.8 studies and Moderna's comparative data remain confidential, so this layering is the strongest defensible reading of a public record incomplete by design [[acknowledgement]]. What stands: freezing necessary, ultra-cold merely fastest-to-validate; m1Ψ awarded for viability, not logistics. Next time, test at deployment temperature, fund the unglamorous excipient and drying layers, and expect the freezer's exit on a regulatory timetable — dried deployed chemistry has beaten six months refrigerated since 2022. The molecule was never as delicate as the first label implied; the paperwork was never as trivial as the word suggests.
