 The authoritative pharmaceutical-science review declines the tempting equation: modified nucleosides improve translation and immunogenicity profiles "but do not, by themselves, confer chemical stability against hydrolysis" — m1Ψ swaps a base, not the backbone [[lock-2]]. Linkage-level help is sign-unpredictable: probing found uridine-upstream hotspots that Ψ/m1Ψ mitigates, mO5U worsened thermal stability versus plain uridine, and AUP-minimized recoding bought a twofold stabilization. Yet no controlled liquid-formulation m1Ψ-versus-unmodified shelf-life trial exists anywhere indexed across 2005–2026, and the era's natural experiment agrees: CureVac's CVnCoV on completely unmodified uridines claimed three months refrigerated anyway [[acknowledgement]] [[references-2]]. Its European rolling review, however, was withdrawn unfinished — a manufacturer claim, not endorsed data [[ema-ends-rolling-review-of-cvncov-covid-19-vaccine-following-withdrawal-by-curev]]. Schoenmaker keeps one door open: indications that m1Ψ increases base stacking and melting point, "thereby making mRNA more stable," possibly affecting pre-administration stability. Verdict: decisive viability and timing credit; single digits to at most ten percent direct storage credit.
 
 ## 4. Formulation-Level Breakthroughs: LNP Encapsulation and Frozen-Stability Engineering
 
-Formulation chemistry changes what the molecule experiences in the vial, and is where margin was physically created. Sucrose was load-bearing: unprotected particles lose over half their potency within two to three freeze–thaw cycles as ice concentrates salts into rupturing pockets, making multi-dose frozen distribution at pandemic scale impossible without cryoprotection — both products shipped frozen in sucrose from day one [[lock-2]]. Lipid identity is a third lever: Reinhart's C12-200- and SM-102-based LNPs looked identically stable — size, dispersity, encapsulation, mRNA content all flat — yet C12-200 held reporter expression eleven weeks at both 2–8 °C and 25 °C while SM-102 faded at 25 °C. Stable specs masked functional loss: potency, not particle metrics, binds shelf life. The Tris swap followed: Comirnaty's phosphate buffer shifts pH catastrophically during freezing, and reformulation into Tris (tromethamine) earned a refrigerated extension "from up to 1 month, to 10 weeks" — roughly 3.3×, the largest chemistry-attributable multiplier, twin-engined by resistance to freeze-induced pH drift and sacrificial aldehyde scavenging [[acknowledgement]]. The record supplies its control: Spikevax carried Tris from inception yet held thirty refrigerated days because its −20 °C depot left less headroom, while Tris-era products hold the field's best refrigerated allowances through the 2025–26 labels [[acknowledgement]] [[lock-2]].
