 ## 6. Opinionated Synthesis: Which Breakthroughs Actually Unlocked the Cold Chain
 
-Line up BNT162b2's labels — tiers running ultracold depot, pharmaceutical freezer, refrigerator, clocked ambient handling — and force each movement to declare what changed physically. From the December 2020 authorization, −80/−60 °C depot and 120 hours refrigerated post-thaw, the window reached ten weeks: fourteen-fold. May 2021's six-fold jump involved zero product change; Tris added ~3.3×; ln(6)/ln(14) puts two-thirds of the expansion in the uncovering column. The regulator's file concurs: finished product authorized at −90/−60 °C on "limited stability data" from essentially one clinical batch, active substance approved at −20 ± 5 °C the same month, warmer-depot investigation formally directed in the initial MA report itself (REC22). The shipping band wraps dry ice sublimating at −78.5 °C, inside the label [[comirnaty-chmp-assessment-report-ema7073832020-initial-ma-19-feb-2021-stability]]. Operationally the envelope meant 72-hour unopened shipper endurance — forcing air freight under dry-ice flight limits — 24 hours of use once a box opened, and 5,000-dose pack-outs that excluded rural sites and poorer countries [[the-coldest-cold-chain-chilling-effects-of-covid-19-vaccines]]; FDA's Peter Marks framed February 2021's relaxation accordingly: less ultra-low freezer procurement, more reachable sites [[coronavirus-covid-19-update-fda-allows-more-flexible-storage-transportation-cond]].
